<title>FRANCE: Thomson-CSF group awarded French foot soldier pact.</title>
<headline>Thomson-CSF group awarded French foot soldier pact.</headline>
<dateline>PARIS 1997-04-28</dateline>
<text>
<p>The French defence procurement agency has awarded an exploratory contract to develop an integrated equipment system for foot soldiers to a group led by defence electronics firm Thomson-CSF, with state-owned Giat industries as joint prime contractor, Thomson-CSF and Giat said on Monday in a joint statement.</p>
<p>Other companies in the group winning the contract, whose value was not given, were Aero International (Regional), Bertin, CGF Gallet, Sextant Avionique, Paul Boye and VTN industries, the firms said in a statement.</p>
<p>The 3.5-year contract is intended to enhance the capabilities of foot soldiers in the field.</p>
<p>The system, intended to weigh less than 27 kg, will consist of 11 elements including a combat outfit, helmet, electronic equipment and assault rifle.</p>
<p>Should the development project succeed, the group eventually expects orders for thousands of the systems.</p>
<p>-- Paris newsroom +331 4221 5452</p>
